@* Shared using directives for every ZenithUI component. _Imports.razor files are additive down
   the directory tree, so each component folder inherits these and only has to declare its
   @namespace.

   This file lives in Components/ rather than at the project root deliberately. A root
   _Imports.razor would generate its class as `ZenithUI._Imports`, colliding with the folder-level
   files that flatten their components into the `ZenithUI` namespace. Keeping it one level down
   gives it the distinct `ZenithUI.Components` namespace and sidesteps the clash. *@

@using System.Globalization
@using System.Linq.Expressions
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using ZenithUI
@using ZenithUI.Core
@using ZenithUI.Services

@* Deliberately absent: @rendermode. A component library must never pick a render mode for the
   host application - the consumer decides whether a page is static, Server or WebAssembly. *@
